// EXPECT: [E128]
// EXPECT-TEXT: 'x' is a member of 'P' of type 'i32', not a function
// A field that holds a value is not callable. `p.x()` was accepted and emitted C that gcc
// rejects: the UFCS check ran only for a member with no type, so a typed member went on as a
// direct call of a member (I.46, found by M13's member-to-call operator).
type P { x i32, y i32 }

func main() i32 {
    var p = P(0, 2)
    return p.x()
}
